      <marc:subfield code="a">&quot;This book offers information and insight on best practices for reference collection management, no matter the size, and shows why managing without a plan is a recipe for clutter and confusion. In this very practical guide, reference librarians will learn: The importance of collection development policies, and how to effectively involve others in the decision-making process. New insights into selecting reference materials, both print and electronic. Strategies for collection maintenance, including the all-important issue of weeding. This important new book will help librarians make better reference decisions, aligned to customer needs and expectations, especially significant with today&apos;s limited budgets.&quot;</marc:subfield>
